# Angular Film Collection — Cursor Rules

## ══════════════════════════════════════════
## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW & HARD CONSTRAINTS
## ══════════════════════════════════════════

This is an Angular 20+ standalone-component application called **Film Collection**.
It is a course submission project — clean, readable, and architecturally correct code matters above all.

### ABSOLUTE PROHIBITIONS — never violate these:
- ❌ NO RxJS — not a single `Observable`, `Subject`, `BehaviorSubject`, `pipe()`, `subscribe()`
- ❌ NO NgModules — every component/pipe/directive must be `standalone: true`
- ❌ NO UI libraries (Angular Material, PrimeNG, etc.)
- ❌ NO `any` type — TypeScript strict mode is ON
- ❌ NO raw DOM access (`document.getElementById`, `querySelector`) outside directives
- ❌ NO logic inside templates beyond simple conditionals
- ❌ NO `setTimeout`/`setInterval` for reactive state (exception: autofocus timing only)
- ❌ NO `*ngFor`, `*ngIf`, `*ngSwitch` structural directives
- ❌ NO `@Input()` / `@Output()` decorators — use `input()` / `output()` functions
- ❌ NO constructor-based dependency injection — always use `inject()`
- ❌ NO `toSignal` / `toObservable` from rxjs-interop — forbidden bridge to RxJS
- ❌ NO `ActivatedRoute` in components — use `input()` with `withComponentInputBinding()`

### MANDATORY TECHNOLOGIES:
- ✅ Angular 20+ with standalone components
- ✅ Angular Signals: `signal()`, `computed()`, `effect()`, `input()`, `output()`
- ✅ New control flow: `@if`, `@for`, `@switch`, `@empty`
- ✅ TypeScript strict mode (`"strict": true` in tsconfig)
- ✅ SCSS for styles (plain — no Tailwind, no Bootstrap)
- ✅ `RouterLink`, `RouterLinkActive` for navigation
- ✅ `withComponentInputBinding()` in `provideRouter` — route params via `input()`

