## ══════════════════════════════════════════
## 8. COMPONENT RULES
## ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Component anatomy — required skeleton:
```typescript
import { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, computed, inject, input, output } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-film-card',
  standalone: true,
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,  // ALWAYS OnPush
  imports: [/* only what this template uses — keep it minimal */],
  templateUrl: './film-card.component.html',
  styleUrl: './film-card.component.scss',
})
export class FilmCardComponent {
  // 1. Inputs (signal-based)
  readonly film = input.required<Film>();

  // 2. Outputs
  readonly favoriteToggled = output<number>();

  // 3. Injected services (private — not accessible in template)
  private readonly filmService = inject(FilmService);

  // 4. Computed / derived state (protected — accessible in template)
  protected readonly isHighRated = computed(() => this.film().rating >= 8);

  // 5. Event handlers (protected)
  protected onToggleFavorite(event: Event): void {
    event.stopPropagation();
    this.favoriteToggled.emit(this.film().id);
  }
}
```

### Smart vs Dumb component pattern — strictly enforced:

| Component | Role | Injects services? | Has `input()`? |
|-----------|------|-------------------|----------------|
| `CatalogComponent` | Smart container | ✅ FilmService, BreadcrumbService | ❌ (it is a route root) |
| `FilmDetailComponent` | Smart container | ✅ FilmService, BreadcrumbService | ✅ `id` from URL |
| `AboutComponent` | Smart container | ✅ BreadcrumbService | ❌ |
| `FilmCardComponent` | Dumb presentational | ❌ NO services | ✅ `film` from parent |
| `HeaderComponent` | Structural | ❌ NO services | ❌ |
| `BreadcrumbsComponent` | Structural | ✅ BreadcrumbService (read-only) | ❌ |
| `FooterComponent` | Structural | ❌ NO services | ❌ |

**Rules:**
- `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` — no exceptions anywhere
- `standalone: true` — no exceptions
- `inject()` function always — never constructor injection
- `input.required<T>()` for mandatory; `input<T>(defaultValue)` for optional
- `protected` for template-facing; `private` for internal-only
- NEVER put business logic in a component — delegate to service
- Selector prefix always `app-`

