## ══════════════════════════════════════════
## 15. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION
## ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Always:
- `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component — no exceptions
- `pure: true` on every pipe (it is the default, but declare it explicitly)
- `track film.id` in `@for` — Angular reuses DOM nodes, skips recreation
- `loadComponent` lazy loading — features bundle separately
- `computed()` for all derived state — cached, re-evaluates only on dependency change
- `readonly` on every signal, computed reference, and injected service
- `loading="lazy"` on `<img>` tags not in the initial viewport

### Never:
```html
<!-- ❌ BAD — method call creates new array on every CD cycle -->
@for (film of getFilteredFilms(); track film.id) { ... }

<!-- ✅ GOOD — computed() result is cached -->
@for (film of filteredFilms(); track film.id) { ... }
```

### How OnPush + Signals work together:
Angular re-checks a component ONLY when:
1. An `input()` signal changes (new reference)
2. A DOM event fires inside the component
3. A signal that the template reads changes (automatic)

Result: maximum performance without manual `markForCheck()` calls.

