## ══════════════════════════════════════════
## 16. SOLID PRINCIPLES IN THIS PROJECT
## ══════════════════════════════════════════

### S — Single Responsibility:
- `FilmService` — film state only (no routing, no formatting, no breadcrumbs)
- `BreadcrumbService` — breadcrumb state only
- `DurationPipe` — duration formatting only
- `AutofocusDirective` — focus behavior only
- `FilmCardComponent` — renders one card, emits one event

### O — Open/Closed:
- Add sorting: new `computed()` in `FilmService`, zero changes to existing code
- Add filter by genre: new `signal()` + `computed()` in `CatalogComponent`
- Components are configurable via `input()` without internal modification

### L — Liskov Substitution:
- Any valid `Film` object works in any component accepting `Film`
- No id-specific conditionals inside `FilmCardComponent`

### I — Interface Segregation:
- `FilmCardComponent` receives `Film` via `input()` — not the whole `FilmService`
- `BreadcrumbsComponent` reads only `crumbs` signal — not any film data

### D — Dependency Inversion:
- Components depend on `Film` interface, not on `FilmService` implementation
- `inject()` makes all dependencies explicit and testable

